{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1017330-how-to-hide-yourself-and-why-it-s-not-possible","id":1017330,"title":"How to hide yourself and why it's not possible","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-14T14:48:10-08:00","id":1017330,"title":"How to hide yourself and why it's not possible","content":"Taking discussion from inappropriate <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016651-reign-of-the-exarchs?p=1017183#post1017183\">thread</a>. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> That's a lovely vision. I like that. But still. Cutting or even veiling your sympathies damages you a lot. - But if you are hiding with master level spell you can expect to be hunted by a master level spell. Corridors of Time will get you before you'll enter your safe spot.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> You do realize that there is a whole chapter about creative thaumaturgy? Rulling let's you do things that can happen and bumping into somene is one of those things. It's what Fate does, you wish something and tadaa.<br /> And well. I hate this little paragraph in Time about using attainmant only with spells that ask for it. It's a throwback to 1ed when you didn't knew the principles behind spell and thus couldn't make your own","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T15:00:23-08:00","id":1017339,"title":"","content":"I wasn't particularly serious, but I can totally see an NPC Mastigos doing that. Perhaps someone the players would have to figure out how to contact in order to gain an important piece of information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T15:15:02-08:00","id":1017346,"title":"","content":"That's exactly what I thought, he would be a good npc but I don't see a way of hiding before 5 dots and even then other masters could hunt you. <br /> Generally speaking I think that you can't hide from from a cabal of your level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T15:27:52-08:00","id":1017352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016651-reign-of-the-exarchs?p=1017335#post1017335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;What Fate does&amp;quot; is allow circumstances to align in a fashion that grants you conveniences as laid out by the confines of the spell's purpose and duration. Fate is not complication-free wishcasting \u2014 you get weird roundabout routes and lucky coincidences, not instant shortcuts around the long-term legwork.<br /> I really, really don't care how much you dislike not being able to run roughshod over the setting based on a failure to read the mechanics. Temporal Sympathy required you to be casting on the subject in the present even before the errata, which doesn't do you much good if they're in a Pocket Dimension you can't access.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was this Gloria Mundis introductory chronicle for 1ed mage. First chapter was giving advice how to find someone and Acanthus had to throw a dart at the map, and that was it. Fate is wishful thinking. I want to have some money - 24 hours later you have some money.<br /> <br /> It did? I must have been idolizing pre-errata Time too much. I should check it I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T16:01:47-08:00","id":1017369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1017330-how-to-hide-yourself-and-why-it-s-not-possible?p=1017352#post1017352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was this Gloria Mundis introductory chronicle for 1ed mage. First chapter was giving advice how to find someone and Acanthus had to throw a dart at the map, and that was it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The task in question was to find his <i>house</i>, the alternative Fate-based method was driving aimlessly, and Adam was unconscious and not actively hiding from the players at the time of that roll, which makes it kind of a shitty example to use for how &quot;impossible&quot; it is to hide from somebody using Fate magic, particularly in the context of &quot;An Adept of Fate, Time, and Space is keeping an Artifact from a pair of second-degree Space Disciples with one dot in Fate between them&quot; that this discussion arose in.<br /> <br /> You wanna bring up Creative Thaum? Veiling spells open up at the same level as &quot;call the phone nearest to the person I'm trying to reach&quot; does and no amount of lucky cartography gets you from Point A to Point B on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T16:26:27-08:00","id":1017381,"title":"","content":"It's also possible to utilize political or personal leverage to gain an advantage the other side may not have. It's also possible to summon up a Supernal entity for an impossible bit of magic or an equally &quot;impossible&quot; artifact that has a power to hide you.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, in a story, the exciting part is pretty much never the hiding and this is a story game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T17:12:37-08:00","id":1017388,"title":"","content":"Notice for future discussions: If you're gonna start up a conversation based on a deviant discussion, it helps to give a brief shakedown of what the conversation is really about. The link is primarily helpful as a way of providing context, but if you're going to do this, you might as well take the step back and re-establish where and what y'all are arguing about.<br /> <br /> Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T18:41:20-08:00","id":1017429,"title":"","content":"You hide like you defend: you don't give someone a reason to find you (or attack you). Or you find them first and attack them first. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T19:04:37-08:00","id":1017437,"title":"","content":"Here's one thing I found tricky in the last game I ran: Exceptional luck grants Informed. I didn't let the Acanthus use it to know everything, but I'm honestly not sure how that kinda boon is supposed to work. I had to informally houserule that Egregore could access rarer information, but it felt like a lot of handwaving. Can Exceptional luck use &quot;Informed&quot; to just locate anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T19:11:54-08:00","id":1017440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1017330-how-to-hide-yourself-and-why-it-s-not-possible?p=1017437#post1017437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's one thing I found tricky in the last game I ran: Exceptional luck grants Informed. I didn't let the Acanthus use it to know everything, but I'm honestly not sure how that kinda boon is supposed to work. I had to informally houserule that Egregore could access rarer information, but it felt like a lot of handwaving. Can Exceptional luck use &quot;Informed&quot; to just locate anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have the Informed Condition lead the mage to someone or something who knows the information. In other words, his Exceptional Luck guides him towards which way he should be looking at, but not what lies at the end of that way. Maybe the mage becomes Informed that <i>someone </i>in the Egregore must know about it or have better means than himself to find about it, or overhears some passerbys chatting about that strange guy they saw yesterday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T19:28:07-08:00","id":1017447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1017330-how-to-hide-yourself-and-why-it-s-not-possible?p=1017440#post1017440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd have the Informed Condition lead the mage to someone or something who knows the information. In other words, his Exceptional Luck guides him towards which way he should be looking at, but not what lies at the end of that way. Maybe the mage becomes Informed that <i>someone </i>in the Egregore must know about it or have better means than himself to find about it, or overhears some passerbys chatting about that strange guy they saw yesterday.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that interpretation. I swear, I spend so much time figuring out how to interpret Exceptional Luck. The only other spell that I had nearly so much trouble with was Shifting Sands. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Edit: It's not a badly written spell. Just requires careful reading. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T02:12:30-08:00","id":1017548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1017330-how-to-hide-yourself-and-why-it-s-not-possible?p=1017429#post1017429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You hide like you defend: you don't give someone a reason to find you (or attack you). Or you find them first and attack them first.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. Once you gave someone a reason to find you - he will. Only masters seem to be able hide from other master as they can create and destroy things entirely. Close yourself in Space prison, destroy your past, create destiny where you can't be found.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T03:17:57-08:00","id":1017565,"title":"","content":"Is that really a problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T03:40:46-08:00","id":1017572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1017330-how-to-hide-yourself-and-why-it-s-not-possible?p=1017565#post1017565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that really a problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this. It was mentioned that Consilia exist for this very reason: <i>to stop mages from killing each other</i>. Even Seers and Libertines, who hate each other's guts, don't drop nukes on each other just because they can - Mutually Assured Destruction, and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T03:44:35-08:00","id":1017573,"title":"","content":"Not really. It's just the thing you need to realize to not make mistakes in writing a plot for your story. I mostly made this thread for people to think of some means of hiding from cabal that is not involving higher dots then they have.<br /> What would be the best way to maximize your chances on disciple level?<br /> -Veiling your sympathy all the time<br /> -Chronos shield<br /> -some kind of occultation granted from Fate to give penalty or clash of will when someone wants to find you with Fate? <br /> -and just to be sure, put some veiling from minds<br /> <br /> Any more ideas how to find a guy and how to protect from it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T03:54:51-08:00","id":1017574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1017330-how-to-hide-yourself-and-why-it-s-not-possible?p=1017573#post1017573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. It's just the thing you need to realize to not make mistakes in writing a plot for your story. I mostly made this thread for people to think of some means of hiding from cabal that is not involving higher dots then they have.<br /> What would be the best way to maximize your chances on disciple level?<br /> -Veiling your sympathy all the time<br /> -Chronos shield<br /> -some kind of occultation granted from Fate to give penalty or clash of will when someone wants to find you with Fate?<br /> -and just to be sure, put some veiling from minds<br /> <br /> Any more ideas how to find a guy and how to protect from it?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Arcana not yet mentioned - Prime to veil your Nimbus from being seen, Forces to stop mundane attempts to track you through electronic and computer devices, Spirit to cover your Resonance-footsteps and enlist the help of spirits of stealth and related concepts, Life to hide your body signs and physical traces left.<br /> <br /> Really, mages have countless methods for both finding some guy and hiding him. I guess the important thing is knowing what the tracker is going to use to track him - Mastigos and Acanthus are obvious, the Obrimos could be reading imprints of magic and heat signatures, the Thyrsus probably has spirit and animal scouts everywhere, and the Moros is doing the same but with ghosts and drones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T04:18:39-08:00","id":1017582,"title":"","content":"If you want a plot about hiding, don't involve other Mages. Like 99% of standard RPG plots that aren't Awakening' strength (Mage has it's own special niche of plots in general), plots based around &quot;hide x&quot; work best when you don't involve non-PC Mages too much. Seriously, human occultists invested with Abyssal Power of their patron will make that kind of plots much more manageable, for example. From a GM/story writer perspective, Magic works best when it's mainly a tool in PC hands, at least until you get a real good understanding of the inside outs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T04:27:16-08:00","id":1017589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1017330-how-to-hide-yourself-and-why-it-s-not-possible?p=1017574#post1017574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the Arcana not yet mentioned - Prime to veil your Nimbus from being seen, Forces to stop mundane attempts to track you through electronic and computer devices, Spirit to cover your Resonance-footsteps and enlist the help of spirits of stealth and related concepts, Life to hide your body signs and physical traces left.<br /> <br /> Really, mages have countless methods for both finding some guy and hiding him. I guess the important thing is knowing what the tracker is going to use to track him - Mastigos and Acanthus are obvious, the Obrimos could be reading imprints of magic and heat signatures, the Thyrsus probably has spirit and animal scouts everywhere, and the Moros is doing the same but with ghosts and drones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nimbus is not a big issue when you are in another city. Forces - yea, I forgot about face recognition software. So you need forces or Life preferably to Veil your face from machines and humans alike. Heat signatures only help you when you are reaally close, basically, you found him and you know he is there. Spirits and animals are nice, I could see it but you need something that smells of or belonged to the chased guy (for ghosts too). <br /> <br /> So the list of Veiling spells gets bigger and bigger. A cabal will find a single mage and that's a fact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> For some reason I didn't notice your earlier posts. Sorry for that.<br /> <br /> Satchel: I'm just saying that you need to have all those veiling spell at the same or higher lvl as the cabal that chases you. If they wan't to they will find you like a Liam Neeson.<br /> \u200b<br /> Mrmdubois: Running from a danger can make a good chapter or even story arc. And yea. It's a good reason to haggle with supernals or even abyss for help. Good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T06:26:39-08:00","id":1017615,"title":"","content":"It can be interesting, trying to hide or run or whatever, but eventually I gets old or becomes the norm for the story at which point it stops mattering as much. Flash points of interest for the story are only going to come up when the hiding is compromised or the enemy catches up to you. That's in fact the entire point of Gawain handing the Ring off to the cabal in narrative terms. They could possibly manage to hide it, but even so you then wouldn't actually get a cool conflict with the Seers.<br /> <br /> Put it another way, successfully hiding is the end of the hiding storyline, only the threat of discovery keeps it unresolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T11:53:02-08:00","id":1017739,"title":"","content":"Imo, the easiest way to hide is to not be directly involved. Use catspaws and third (or fourth, or fifth, etc.) parties to do the hands on work. So yea, they might know that there's <i>someone</i> pulling the strings, but it gives you a lot of room for misdirection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}